This form is probably a rather late innovation in the Northern region, displaced {{m|vi|bổn}} in the Northern dialects:
* ''bản'' as the Sino-Vietnamese reading of {{ltc-l|本}} is attested once (as {{m|mkh-mvi|bản đạo}}) in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'', a dictionary chiefly based on the Northern dialects, while {{m|vi|bổn}} is attested thrice (in {{m|mkh-mvi|bổn đạo||of the same religion}}, {{m|mkh-mvi|bổn cục||a circle of craftsmen}}, {{m|mkh-mvi|nhịt bổn||Japan}}).
* The expected Sino-Vietnamese reflex for this rime is {{IPAfont|/on/}}, cf. {{m|vi|bôn}} < {{ltc-l|奔|id=1}}, {{m|vi|bồn}} < {{ltc-l|盆}}, {{m|vi|bộn}} < {{ltc-l|坌}}.
* In early Nôm texts (which are all of clear Northern origin), {{ltc-l|本}} was used as a phonogram or as the phonetic in phono-semantograms to write the native Vietnamese word {{m|vi|bốn||four}}, whose vocalism value is stable throughout its development from Proto-Vietic to Modern Vietnamese.

