====Usage notes====
* Depending on the scheme, "Central Vietnamese" can be variously defined, but always includes the North Central dialects from certain parts of {{w|Thanh Hoá province|Thanh Hoá}} southwards to {{w|Huế}}. In linguistic literature, the South Central dialects of {{w|Đà Nẵng}}-{{w|Quảng Nam}}-{{w|Quảng Ngãi province|Quảng Ngãi}} can be seen included within Southern Vietnamese (see Tooyama (2018)'s treatise on dialects of Quảng Nam),<ref>Tooyama (通山), Emi (絵美). 2018. [https://ir.library.osaka-u.ac.jp/repo/ouka/all/72344/30336_Dissertation.pdf ベトナム語クアンナム方言の音韻に関する共時的・通時的研究]. Osaka University, PhD thesis.</ref> yet these dialects have features (both conservative and innovative) align with the North Central dialects. On the other hand, the {{m|vi|Nẫu}} dialects of {{w|Bình Định}} and {{w|Phú Yên}} are sometimes subsumed in Central Vietnamese by laymen, although they have far fewer Central features.

