chiều.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-chiều.wav|a=Hanoi}}

===Etymology 1===
{{rfe|vi|
Probably of foreign origin: 
* 𪤾 is just another phonosemantic compound, with phonetic 朝 & semantic 夕 "evening";
* Derivation from {{ltc-l|朝|id=1}} (> SV. triêu) "morning > daytime, full day" is not plausible due to its lack of parsimony, requiring one to assume: 
** misreading of triêu as triều to account for register mismatch (however, see {{m|vi|thính#Etymology 2|thính}}) and 
** semantic shift from "morning > daytime, full day" to "late after; early evening", not present in Chinese;
* Derivation from {{ltc-l|朝|id=2}} (> SV. triều) "to face, towards" is plausible, considering the compounds xế chiều (whose xế originally means "slanting, inclined") and chiều tà (whose tà originally means "slanting, inclined"), both pretty indicative of the likelihood of 朝 in its verbal form.

Compare also {{ltc-l|晝|daytime, daylight}} → SV. ''trú''.}}

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|[[朝]], [[𣊿]], [[𣋂]], [[𣎢]], [[𪤾]], [[𫠧]], [[𬩕]]|rdp=chiều chiều}}

