As the Gregorian calendar has displaced the Vietnamese lunisolar calendar as a civil calendar, this word has become more closely associated with the former's seven-day week than the latter's ten-day week. {{m|vi|tuần lễ|Tuần lễ}} is often used for clarity or emphasis.

