tắt.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*p-sət}} ~ {{m|mkh-vie-pro|*p-sat}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|-}} Bi {{m|mtq|thắt}}, {{cog|scb|-}} [Rục] ''pəsat⁷''. Also compare {{cog|zng|hat⁷||to turn off}} (from earlier ''*s-'' through regular debuccalization in Mang), {{cog|kdt|-}} [Souei] ''pəsat'' ("to extinguish").

Unlikely to be related to {{ncog|mkh-ban-pro|*pat||to extinguish}}, {{ncog|mkh-kat-pro|*pat||extinguished (of fire)}}, {{ncog|mkh-khm-pro|*-pət||to extinguish}}, unless there was an infix {{IPAfont|*-s-}} (which is otherwise unknown within Austroasiatic) or metathesis of a presyllable ({{IPAfont|*s-p- > *p-s-}}). The first scenario can almost be safely disregarded, but the second is slightly more plausible since this root is attested both on its own and accompanied by presyllables and/or prefixes across Austroasiatic branches, plus the existence of the Souei cognate above. Still, it might just be coincidental.

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|[[必]], [[𢴑]], [[㴽]], [[𤎕]], [[熄]], [[⿰滅悉]]}}

# {{lb|vi|ambitransitive}} {{q|of [[fire]]}} to be [[out]]; to [[put out]]; {{q|of [[light]] source}} to stop [[glow]]ing
#: {{coa|vi|lửa '''tắt''' ngúm|the fire '''is''' completely '''out'''}}
#: {{coa|vi|nắng '''tắt'''|the sun sets|lit=the sunlight '''fades'''}}
# to [[switch off]], [[turn off]], [[shut down]]
#: {{ant|vi|bật}}
#: {{coa|vi|'''tắt''' ti vi|to '''turn off''' the TV}}
