===Etymology===
{{rfe|vi}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=[[con]], [[cái]]}}

# the [[narrow]] [[space]] between two [[large]] [[barrier]]s
#: {{uxi|vi|hẻm vực|a canyon}}
#: {{uxi|vi|hẻm núi|the space between two mountains}}
# {{lb|vi|by extension}} a [[cul-de-sac]] {{gl|blind alley}}

====Usage notes====
* ''hẻm'' in Vietnam are (usually narrow) roads that lead to a dead end, and they are numbered, not named like open streets. Some streets that are so tight they're not eligible for being named and covered in asphalt may also be considered "''hẻm''".
* Unlike true alleys, which are often concrete walkways or footpaths, ''hẻm'' can still be paved with asphalt and open for vehicular traffic.
* For a figurative "dead end", use {{m|vi|ngõ cụt}} instead.

===Adjective===
{{vi-adj}}

# {{lb|vi|of an [[alley]]}} [[narrow]]

