về.raw:
===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Penn Zero MSSJ-về.wav|a=Hanoi}}
* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-về.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*veːr||to [[return]]}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*wi:r||to go around, to return}}. Cognate with {{cog|mtq|wềl}}, {{cog|kjg|-}} ''wer'' ("to roll, to turn to the opposite end") and {{cog|km|វេរ}}. {{doublet|vi|quê}} through a prefixed protoform.

Most prepositions in Vietnamese were originally verbs: {{m|vi|ở||to stay; at, in}}, {{m|vi|đến||to come; to}}, {{m|vi|tới||to arrive; to}}, {{m|vi|lên||to go up; onto}}, {{m|vi|vào||to enter; in, into}}, {{m|vi|theo||to follow; according to}}, {{m|vi|cho||to give; for}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|vi|viền|q1=North Central Vietnam|pos=in dialects where {{IPAfont|*-l > /n/}}}}
* {{alt|vi|dìa|q1=Nẫu}}

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|[[𧗱]], [[衛]], [[𫟘]], [[𱸳]], [[𲀛]], [[𬩍]], [[𡗅]]}}

# to [[come back]] or [[go back]] (to somewhere one [[belong]]s or to some place that is one's own)
#: {{coi|vi|'''về''' nhà|to '''return''' home}}
#: {{coi|vi|'''về''' quê|to '''return''' to '''one's''' hometown}}
#: {{coi|vi|'''về''' nước|to '''return''' to '''one's''' country}}
#: {{uxi|vi|'''về''' khách sạn|'''to go back''' to the hotel '''where one is currently staying'''}}
#: {{uxi|vi|trên đường '''về''' nhà|headed '''back''' home}}
#: {{uxi|vi|hướng '''về''' Hà Tĩnh|to be headed '''back (home) to''' Hà Tĩnh}}
#: {{coi|vi|'''về''' phía|toward the direction in question; as for}}
#* '''1922''', Hồ Biểu Chánh, ''Ai làm được'', Tín Đức Thư xã, chapter 3
#*: {{quote|vi|Chí Ðại lo sợ nên đi tối ngày không '''về''' nhà.
|translation=Chí Đại was worried, so for the entire day he was away and did not '''return''' home.}}
#* {{quote-text|vi|year=1956|author=Nam Cao|title=Sống mòn|publisher=Văn nghệ|section=part X
|passage=Vợ Mô đi làm '''về''', tạt qua sân, đi thẳng vào bếp của ngôi nhà lá.
|translation=Mô's wife '''came back''' from work, crossed the yard, and went straight to the kitchen of the leaf-covered hut.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* To express returning to a place that is not one's own, such as someone else's home or country, one can use {{m|vi|quay lại}}, {{m|vi|trở lại}}, {{m|vi|[[lại]] [[đến]]}}, and the like.
* To express coming back from a certain activity, the word ''về'' is normally placed after the verb describing that activity, such as
*: {{uxi|vi|đi chơi '''về'''|to '''go back home''' after going out}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|vi|trở về|về vườn|về chuồng|đi về|về hưu|bài tập về nhà}}

====Preposition====
{{vi-prep}}

# [[about]]; [[on]]
#: {{ux|vi|Tôi đã suy nghĩ '''về''' cô ấy.|I have been thinking '''about''' her.}}
#: {{ux|vi|lo lắng '''về''' sức khỏe|worry '''about''' health}}
# [[into]]
#: {{ux|vi|Các phòng trưng bày nghệ thuật mở cửa '''về''' khuya.|All the art galleries are open late '''into''' the night.}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{vi-noun}}

# {{lb|vi|Southern Vietnam}} [[thick]] [[layer]]
#: {{ux|vi|Trứng muỗi nở ra [[lăng quăng]], nổi trên mặt nước thành từng '''về''' lớn trong điều kiện yên tĩnh.|Mosquito eggs hatch into larvae that form a '''thick layer''' floating near the surface when the water is calm.}}

