giấy.raw:
{{wp|vi:}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|vi|q=North Central Vietnam|chấy}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*k-cajʔ}}, from a descendant of reconstructed {{der|vi|och|-}} {{och-l|紙|tr=*k.teʔ}} when the dental stop already palatalized. Attested as {{m|mkh-mvi|gếy}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651). Cognate with {{cog|aem|-}} ''kacajˀ'' ("book"), {{cog|mtq|chẩy|t=paper}}; {{vi-etym-sino|hv=preMC|紙|paper|chỉ|nocap=y}}.

The same sound change also yields Vietnamese {{l|vi|giống}}, from Proto-Vietic {{l|mkh-vie-pro|*k-coːŋʔ}}, from a descendant of ultimately Old Chinese {{och-l|種|tr=*k.toŋʔ}}.

For another word with similar phonological development, see {{m|vi|giặc}}, from {{m|zh|賊}}. Also compare {{cog|lbc|-}} ''kʰjei²⁴'' ("paper") and ''kjak²⁴'' ("thief"), borrowed from the same sources.

