* {{alt|vi|trựa|q1=North Central Vietnam|pos=dialects with ''ngã''-''nặng'' merger}}

===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|tou|-}} [Cuối Chăm] ''kʰrɐː⁶''.

The mainstream Vietnamese form underwent the uncommon but attested {{IPAfont|*C-r- >}} ‹gi-› shift instead of regular {{IPAfont|*C-r- >}} ‹s-›. The North Central forms exhibit the local frequent shift {{IPAfont|*C-r- > *C-l-}}. For the correspondence, compare mainstream {{m|vi|già}} vs. North Central {{m|vi|tra||old}}, mainstream {{m|vi|giòi}} vs. North Central {{m|vi|troi||maggot}}.

Northern Old Vietnamese in the earliest Nôm texts in  already showed cluster simplification (with its usage of {{ltc-l|字}} as phonetic), while the contemporary Old Vietnamese form ancestral to the modern North Central forms certainly still had the consonant cluster at the time.

