# {{lang|vi|([[hoa]], [[bông]] ~)}} [[rose]] ({{taxfmt|Rosa|genus}})
#* {{quote-book|vi|origlang=en|year= 2006|origyear= 1597|author= w:William Shakespeare|title= William Shakespeare – Tuyển Tập Tác Phẩm|trans-title= William Shakespeare – Selected Works|chapter= w:Romeo and Juliet|translator= Đặng Thế Bính|origtext= en:What's in a name ? that which we call a '''rose''', By any other name would smell as sweet; [...]|text= Cái tên nào có nghĩa gì? Bông '''hồng''' kia, giá gọi bằng một tên khác, thì hương thơm cũng vẫn ngạt ngào.|page= 82|pageurl= https://archive.org/details/vh.tuyentaptacphamwilliamshakespeare/page/82/mode/2up}}
#* '''1842''', {{w|Karl Marx}}, [http://www.mlwerke.de/me/me01/me01_060.htm “Fünfter Artikel (Fifth Article)”] in ''Debatten über Preßfreiheit und Publikation der Landständischen Verhandlungen (Debates on Freedom of the Press and Publication of the Proceedings of the Assembly of the Estates)''; '''2010''' [1975] English translation from ''{{w|Marx/Engels Collected Works}}'', “Vol. 1”<!--- page numbered 164 --->; '''1995''' Vietnamese translation from ''C. Mác Và Ph. Ăng-ghen Toàn Tập [K. Marx & F. Engels Complete Works]'', [https://tulieuvankien.dangcongsan.vn/c-mac-angghen-lenin-ho-chi-minh/book/ph-angghen/tac-pham/c-mac-va-ph-angghen-toan-tap-tap-1-183 “Vol.  1”]<!--- unnumbered 76th page --->
#*: {{ux|vi|'''Hồng''' nào mà chẳng có gai! Nhưng, xin các vị hãy nghĩ xem, các vị bị mất gì cùng với báo chí tự do!|You cannot pluck the '''rose''' without its thorns! And what do you lose with a free press?|lit= Which '''rose''' has no thorn? Still, just you think! What do you lose with a free press?}}

====Usage notes====
* When used alone, '''hồng''' almost always denotes persimmons, and only on rare occasions does '''hồng''' denote roses.
* When used to denote roses, '''hồng''' is almost always preceded by the {{w|Classifier (linguistics)|classifier}} ''{{l|vi|đoá}}'' (resulting in "đoá hồng"), the noun ''{{l|vi|bông}}'' or ''{{l|vi|hoa}}'' (resulting in "hoa hồng" or "bông hồng"), or both ''đoá'' then any of those nouns (resulting in "đoá hoa hồng" or "đoá bông hồng"); even so, note that ''bông'' functions as a classifier in the expression "bông hoa hồng".
* To denote rose plants, either ''hoa'' or ''bông'' is required after classifier ''cây'' (resulting in "cây bông hồng" or "cây hoa hồng"). On the other hand, when preceded by ''đoá'', ''bông'', ''hoa'', {{m|vi|nụ||bud}}, {{m|vi|cánh||petal}}, or {{m|vi|cành}}, {{m|vi|nhành}}, {{m|vi|nhánh}} (the last three meaning "{{q|[[botany]]}} [[branch]]"), '''hồng''' denotes roses, not persimmons.

====See also====
* {{l|vi|thị||yellow persimmon, ''Diospyros decandra''}}
* {{l|vi|cậy||date-plum, ''Diospyros lotus''}}

{{C|vi|Ebony family plants|Fruits|Pinks|Reds}}

