Similarities to {{ncog|zh|-}} {{och-l|勁|tr={{IPAfont|*keŋ-s}}}} (SV: {{m|vi|kình}}, {{m|vi|kính}}), {{och-l|強|tr={{IPAfont|*N-kaŋ, *m-kaŋʔ}}}} (SV: {{m|vi|cường}}, {{m|vi|cưỡng}}), {{och-l|剛|tr={{IPAfont|*kˤaŋ}}}} (SV: {{m|vi|cương}}), {{och-l|堅|tr={{IPAfont|*kˤi[ŋ]}}}} (SV: {{m|vi|kiên}}) are probably coincidental. The Austroasiatic words might also be borrowed from another source that gave rise to one of the Sinitic words.

