dưa hấu.raw:
===Etymology===
According to the Vietnamese folktale [[s:vi:Sự tích trái dưa hấu|''Sự tích trái dưa hấu'']] (''Legend of the Watermelon''), the name ''dưa hấu'' derives from {{m|vi|dưa||[[melon]]}} + a non-Sino-Vietnamese reading of {{m|zh|好}} ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|hảo}}), but this is most likely just [[folk etymology]].

Compare also {{zh-l|*煦}} (SV: ''hú''), which has an uncommon meaning {{lang|zh|赤}} "red" (according to ''{{w|Shuowen Jiezi}}'' and ''{{w|Yupian}}''<ref>《康熙字典·火部·九》[https://kangxizidian.com/search/index.php?stype=Word&sword=%E7%85%A6&detail=y 煦]; quote: (又《說文》一曰'''赤'''貌。《玉篇》'''赤'''色也。) </ref>) and one of whose Old Chinese pronunciations was *''qʰoʔ'' ({{w|Reconstructions_of_Old_Chinese#Zhengzhang_(1981–1995)|ZS}}). If ''hấu'' indeed reflexed {{och-l|煦|id=1}}, then '''dưa hấu''' would have been a compound of {{com|vi|dưa|t1= melon|alt2= hấu}} ("red {{q|obsolete}}"), the latter referring to the color of the fruit's fresh.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=[[trái]], [[quả]]}}

# [[watermelon]]

===References===
