===Etymology===
Often explained as being derived from {{com|vi|bánh|đa|t1=any [[sweet]], [[salty]], or [[savory]] [[food]] prepared from [[flour]]|t2=[[banyan]]}}, from the supposed resemblance of the rice paper to a banyan leaf.

This name was the result of a [[taboo]]-induced lexical replacement of the preexisting {{m|vi|bánh tráng}}, during Lord {{w|Trịnh Tráng}}'s rule of Northern Vietnam (1623–1654), when there was {{w|naming taboo}} of Tráng's name. The original term is now preserved in areas of Central and Southern Vietnam, which were not under the reign of Lord Trịnh Tráng at the time.

