===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|報||hv=n|báo}}. {{doublet|vi|báo}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|vi|biểu|q=South Central Vietnam, Southern Vietnam}}

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|[[保]], [[𠸒]]}}

# to [[inform]]; to [[command]] by [[telling]]
#: {{ux|vi|Lại đây mẹ '''bảo'''.|Come here, I got something to '''tell''' you. / I got something I want you to do.}}
#: {{ux|vi|Nó '''bảo''' thứ hai nghỉ.|She '''told''' me we don't need to come on Monday.}}
#: {{ux|vi|Đã '''bảo''' rồi!|'''Told''' you!}}
#: {{ux|vi|'''Bảo''' sao nghe vậy.|I'm only doing what I'm told to do. / I'm only following orders.|lit=I'm listening to what I'm '''told'''.}}
#: {{ux|vi|Có câm không thì '''bảo''' !|Shut the hell up or else!|lit=Shut up or I'll '''tell''' you to!}}

=====Usage notes=====
{{box-top|Grammar}}
*If {{m|vi|nói||to say; to utter; to talk; to speak}} is grammatically analogous to {{ncog|en|say}} in that it has an "indirect object" which follows {{m|vi|với||to}}, then {{m|vi|bảo}} is analogous to {{ncog|en|tell}} in that it does not require {{m|vi||với}}:
:: {{ux|vi|Em '''nói với''' anh…|I '''said to''' you…}}
:: {{ux|vi|Em bảo anh…|I told you…}}
*There are some cases where a pronoun can be mistaken for an "indirect object" of {{m|vi|nói}}:
:: {{ux|vi|Em nói anh nghe.|I'm telling you this.}}
: This sentence can be changed into {{m|vi||Em nói '''cho''' anh nghe|lit=I'm saying '''so that''' you hear.}}. The verb {{m|vi|nghe||to hear}} is a clue that {{m|vi|anh||you}} is not merely an "object", but actually the subject of a different clause.
{{box-bottom}}

