tay.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-mvi|tay}}, from {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*siː}}. Cognate with {{cog|tou|-}} [Cuối Chăm] ''siː¹'', {{cog|thm|ซี}}.

The relationship between this root and the root represented by {{cog|km|ដៃ}}, {{cog|bdq|ti}}, {{cog|jun|-}} ''iti'' is uncertain. {{cog|srb|-}} ''siˀi'' is likely a post-Proto-Munda development, as other Munda reflexes show {{IPAfont|/t/}}.

The "Northern" Austroasiatic branches (Khmuic, Palaungic, Khasian) occasionally show forms with a fricative, affricate, or palatal stop that correspond to {{IPAfont|*t}} in the non-Northern branches. Vietic, as a non-"Northern" branch, shows alveolar stop (cf. {{ncog|kjg|-}} [Cuang] ''caŋ'' vs. Vietnamese {{m|vi|đắng||bitter}}, {{ncog|mlf|-}} ''sam'' vs. Vietnamese {{m|vi|đăm||right}}, possibly {{ncog|kjg|-}} [Cuang] ''psɨəm'' vs. Vietnamese {{m|vi|đêm||night}}). Yet here, the "Northern" branches all show {{IPAfont|/t/}} ({{ncog|kjg|-}} [Cuang] ''tiʔ'', {{ncog|prk|taix}}, {{cog|kha|kti}}), but Vietic languages uniformly point to {{IPAfont|*s}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}
