Compare {{cog|mkh-kat-pro|*kpias||lychee}} (whence {{cog|pac|cupiêih}}).

Unlike what some modern sources seem to suggest, there is little to no evidence that ''lệ chi'' ({{m|zh|荔枝}}) was used as a word for "lychee" in Vietnamese, even historically. This confusion is most likely due speakers' conflation between Written Chinese texts and actual Vietnamese texts.

