cánh.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*kɛːŋʔ}}, from {{inh|vi|aav-pro|*kiəŋ||elbow}} (not listed in Sidwell (2024) but compare {{ncog|aav-pro|*miəŋˀ||mouth}} (whence {{m|vi|miếng}}/{{m|vi|mánh}})).

''Đại Nam Quấc âm tự vị'' (1895) records the now obsolete form written as {{m|vi|kiến}}. Considering that this dictionary is based on Southern Vietnamese when the {{IPAfont|/n > ŋ/}} shift already occurred, the form intended here would be etymologically spelled as {{m|vi|kiếng}} (cf. the "{{m|vi|kiếng|kiến}}" for "glass" entry right below). This ''kiếng''/''cánh'' pair represents the diphthongized and undiphthongized variants respectively, in the same vein of {{m|vi|miếng}}/{{m|vi|mánh}}.

