quốc tế.raw:
===Alternative forms===
*{{alt|vi|quốc-tế}}

===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|國|country|際|between}}, from {{bor|vi|ja|国際|tr=kokusai||international}}, clipped from {{der|vi|zh|[[各國]][[交際]]|tr={{m|vi|các quốc [[giao tế]]}}|lit=intercourse between countries}},<ref>{{cite-web|ja|titleurl=https://kotobank.jp/word/%E5%9B%BD%E9%9A%9B-499184#w-499184|work=コトバンク|trans-work=Kotobank|title=国際}}</ref><ref name=wikiversity>{{cite-web|zh|titleurl=https://zh.wikiversity.org/wiki/Subject:%E8%8F%AF%E8%A3%BD%E6%96%B0%E6%BC%A2%E8%AA%9E%E5%8F%8A%E4%B8%AD%E6%96%87%E5%9B%BA%E6%9C%89%E8%AA%9E/%E5%85%B6%E4%BB%96%E7%94%A8%E8%A9%9E|work=維基學院|trans-work=Wikiversity|title=Subject:華製新漢語及中文固有語/其他用詞}}</ref> calqued from {{der|vi|en||diplomatic intercourse}} in the Chinese translation of ''{{w|Elements of International Law}}''. {{m|ja|国際|tr=kokusai}} was used to translate "international" sometime in 1897 Meiji Japan. The original Chinese word for "international" was evidently {{m|zh|萬國|tr={{m|vi|vạn quốc}}|lit=myriad countries}}<ref name=wikiversity/> as in the Chinese title {{m|zh|萬國公法|tr=vạn quốc công pháp|lit=The Public Law of a Myriad Countries}}, or simply {{m|zh|各國|tr=các quốc|lit=countries}}. Another Meiji coinage for "diplomatic intercourse" was {{ncog|ja|[[外国]][[交際]]|tr=gaikoku kōsai, {{m|vi|[[ngoại quốc]] giao tế}}|lit=intercourse with foreign countries}}, which was clipped into {{m|ja|外交|tr=gaikō, {{m|vi|ngoại giao}}}}.

