thôi.raw:
{{was fwotd|vi|2022|December|20}}

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|退|hv=n||[[thối]], [[thoái]]}}.

For the tonal correspondence, see other post-reconstructed Old Chinese, pre-Middle Chinese loans such as {{m|vi|bèn}}, {{m|vi|buôn}}, {{m|vi|chung}}, {{m|vi|cùng}}, where words with Vietnamese A/{{l|vi|bằng}} tones correspond to Qieyun system tone C/{{l|zh|去聲}}. Particularly compare {{m|vi|đôi||pair}}, which exhibits the exact same correspondence in the rime as with ''thôi''.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|vi|thâu|q1=Nẫu}}
* {{alt|vi|thui|q1=Internet slang, text messaging}}

====Noun====
{{vi-noun|[[催]], [[崔]], [[推]], [[傕]]}}

# a [[long]] [[while]]

====Verb====
{{vi-verb|[[催]], [[崔]], [[推]], [[傕]]}}

# to [[stop]] (forever); to [[cease]]; to [[discontinue]]; to [[quit]]
#* {{quote-book|vi|year=1957|author=w:vi:Đoàn Giỏi|title=Đất rừng phương Nam|publisher=w:Kim Đồng Publishing House|chapter=2|text=Thấy tôi không muốn nói, bà ta cũng '''thôi''' không hỏi.|translation=Seeing that I didn't want to tell, she also '''stopped''' asking.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|vi|một thôi một hồi|thôi nôi|thôi được}}

====Interjection====
{{vi-interjection|[[催]], [[崔]], [[推]], [[傕]]}}

# {{n-g|Used [[sentence]]-[[initially]] to [[express]] a [[polite]] [[negative]]:}} [[that's it]]; [[enough]]

====Particle====
{{vi-particle|[[催]], [[崔]], [[推]], [[傕]]}}

# {{lb|vi|colloquial|used sentence-[[finally]]}} [[that's all]]; [[merely]]; [[only]]; [[just]]
# {{lb|vi|colloquial|used sentence-[[initial]]ly}}  {{non-gloss|introduces a new statement that contradicts previously stated statement(s)}}

====Usage notes====
{{sense|particle}}
* As a particle used initially in sentences, ''thôi'' is often used with {{m|vi|mà}} and {{m|vi|thì}}, as {{m|vi|mà thôi}} and {{m|vi|thôi thì}}.
* Also, when used as a sentence-initial particle, the sentence-final particles {{m|vi|đi}} and ''thôi'' ("that's all; merely; only") are usually utilized to clarify the quantity mentioned in the new statement compared to the previous statement:
*: {{ux|vi|'''Thôi''' cho hai phần đi.|On second thought, I want to order two portions (I originally ordered just one portion).}}
*: {{ux|vi|'''Thôi''' cho hai phần thôi.|On second thought, I want to order two portions (I originally ordered three or more portions).}}
{{sense|pronunciation}}
* Colloquially, ''thôi'' is one of the instances where aspirated stops sometimes shift into just /h/ in Vietnamese, so that ''thôi'' is pronounced as ''hôi''. Compare also {{m|vi|hông}} (from {{m|vi|không}}).
* Sometimes deliberately spelled {{m|vi|thui}} to convey informality on the Internet although the word is rarely (if ever) pronounced as such in real life. Compare {{m|vi|rùi}} (from {{m|vi|rồi}}).

===Etymology 2===
{{rfe|vi|Possibly a {{vi-etym-sino|褪||hv=n|thoái}}, not sure though.}}

