* {{audio|vi|LL-Q9199 (vie)-Jessica Nguyen (Pamputt)-phần.wav|a=Ho Chi Minh City}}

===Etymology 1===
{{vi-etym-sino|分|part; portion}}, {{m|vi|份}}, from {{der|vi|ltc|分|tr=bjunH}}, {{m|ltc|份|tr=bjunH}}.

The {{m|vi|huyền}} tone here is rather problematic. The regular tone derivation pattern, based on the original Middle Chinese tone and onset consonant would be as follows:

* {{m|ltc|分|tr=bjunH||portion|pos={{m|zh|去聲||departing tone}}, {{m|zh|[[全濁]][[聲母]]||voiced obstruent onset}}}} > {{cog|vi|phận}}, {{cog|cmn|分|tr=fèn}}, {{cog|yue|分|tr=fan6}}
* {{m|ltc|分|tr=pjun||to divide|pos={{m|zh|平聲||level tone}}, {{m|zh|[[清]][[聲母]]||voiceless obstruent onset}}}} > {{cog|vi|phân}}, {{cog|cmn|分|tr=fēn}}, {{cog|yue|分|tr=fan1}}

The {{m|vi|huyền}} tone suggests an unattested Middle Chinese reading:
* {{m|ltc|分|tr=*bjun||portion|pos=level tone, voiced obstruent onset}} > {{cog|vi|phần}}

Alternatively, the {{m|vi|huyền}} tone suggests non-Classical Chinese origin. Compare {{m|vi|hè}} and {{m|vi|hạ}}, {{m|vi|mùi}} and {{m|vi|vị}}, {{m|vi|vì}} and {{m|vi|vị}}.

{{doublet|vi|phân|phận}}. Cognate with {{cog|cmn|分|tr=fèn}} and {{cog|yue|分|tr=fan6}}. See also {{m|vi|phần tử}} and {{m|vi|phân tử}}, and {{m|vi|Phần Lan}}.

