phổi.raw:
===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*p-soːs||lungs}}, from {{inh|vi|mkh-pro|-}}. In the more innovative Vietic languages, {{IPAfont|*-s-}} debuccalized into {{IPAfont|*-h-}}, then developed regularly to the current Vietnamese form. In this particular case, this {{IPAfont|*-s- > *-h-}} shift might also have been influenced by sound symbolism. Cognate with {{cog|tou|-}} [Cuối Chăm] ''pʰɔːl⁵'', {{cog|thm||pasuh¹}}, {{cog|pac|xóh}}, {{cog|bdq|dơsoh}}, {{cog|mnw|ကသံ|tr=kəsɔˀ}}.

Medial {{IPAfont|*-s-}} has the tendency to debuccalize among Austroasiatic languages, compare {{ncog|mkh-kat-pro|*psaj}}, {{m|mkh-kat-pro|*phaj||otter}} (cognate with {{cog|mkh-vie-pro|*p-seːʔ}}), where conservative {{IPAfont|*-s-}} and innovative {{IPAfont|*-h-}} can both be reconstructed; the other Austroasiatic languages have innovative {{IPAfont|*-h-}}, e.g. {{ncog|km|ភេ}}. Compare also {{ncog|mkh-kat-pro|*ksaj||moon}} vs. {{ncog|mkh-ban-pro|*khaj||moon}}, {{ncog|km|ខែ}}, {{ncog|mkh-vie-pro|*saːmʔ||eight}} vs. {{cog|mkh-ban-pro|*t(n)haːm||eight}}.

Unrelated genetically to {{ncog|zh|-}} {{och-l|肺|tr={{IPAfont|*pʰo[t]-s}}}} (B-S) ([[Sino-Vietnamese|SV]]: {{m|vi|phế}}), although there might had been contamination.

===Pronunciation===
{{vi-IPA}}

===Noun===
{{vi-noun|cls=[[lá]], [[quả]]|[[𦟊]], [[肺]], [[配]], [[𦡮]]}}

# [[lung]]

