===Etymology===
{{vi-etym-sino|解|preMC=y|to [[loosen]]; to [[untie]]; to [[unfasten]]; etc.|giải}}.

Its velar initial and rime suggest it was borrowed from a post-Old Chinese but pre-Middle Chinese layer; meanwhile, {{m|vi|hỏi}}-tone, instead of expected **{{m|vi|sắc}} typical of early loans, hints that its ancestor retained the meanings of tone-B {{zh-l|*解}} yet acquired the reading of tone-C {{zh-l|*解|to pawn, to mortgage; to introduce a scholar to the imperial palace; to send under escort; etc.}} (see {{m|vi|thính}}, {{m|vi|tỉnh}}, {{m|vi|sảnh}}, etc. for analogies).

