{{examples|{{m|vi|𳁓|tr=quan}}, originally written as {{m|vi|觀}}, but the {{lang|vi|雚}} component was replaced with the dot and bend.</br>{{m|vi|𱍬|tr=quét}}, originally written as {{m|vi|𪩺}}, but the {{lang|vi|帚}} component was replaced with the dot and bend.</br>{{m|vi|𱻉|tr=còn}}, originally written as {{m|vi|群}}, but the {{lang|vi|君}} component was replaced with the dot and bend.</br>{{m|vi|𱘫|tr=nhiều}}, originally written as {{m|vi|𬲢}}, but the {{lang|vi|飠}} component was replaced with the dot and bend.}}
[[File:鑄 chấm phẩy.png|thumb|An example of a chấm phẩy abbreviation of 鑄. The 釒 radical is replaced with a dot and bend.]]

====Noun====
{{vi-noun}}

# {{lb|vi|historical}} abbreviation of a character by replacing a component of a character with a dot and bend stroke (𬼀).
#* {{quote-book|vi|title=Chữ Hán dị thể ở Việt Nam|trans-title=Chinese character variants in Vietnam|publisher=Thế Giới Publishers|author=Trịnh Khắc Mạnh|year=2024|page=123|passage=Đỗ Thị Bích Tuyển (trong "Graphic abbreviation of Chinese characters in Vietnam: A case study of “dot and bend” in Sino-Nom texts") gọi "𬼀" là "dot and bend" ('''chấm phẩy''') và cho rằng phù hiệu này là kí tự viết tắt của 錢, 饒, 食, 金, 君, 镸, 雚.|translation=Đỗ Thị Bích Tuyển (in "Graphic abbreviation of Chinese characters in Vietnam: A case study of “dot and bend” in Sino-Nom texts") calls "𬼀" a "dot and bend" and considers that this symbol is an abbreviated character for 錢, 饒, 食, 金, 君, 镸, and 雚.}}

