* {{alt|vi|q=North Central Vietnam|tru|pos=no diphthongization}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|vi|mkh-vie-pro|*c-luː}}. Cognate with North Central Vietnamese {{m|vi|tru}}, {{cog|mtq|tlu}}, {{cog|omx|jlow||ox, bull, cattle}} (whence {{cog|mnw|ဂၠဴ}}, {{cog|cbn|-}} ''chǝlòw''), {{cog|zng|løː⁶}} and {{cog|pnx|-}} ''jlǝːw''. 

Attested as Northern {{cog|mkh-mvi|tlâu}} in the ''Dictionarium Annamiticum Lusitanum et Latinum'' (1651). The modern North Central forms are not reflexes of this form, but descended from an unattested non-Northern Middle Vietnamese form.

{{cog|km|ឆ្លូវ||Year of the Ox}} was borrowed from a Vietic variety, and thus is not an inherited cognate of the terms listed above.

