{{rfe|vi|Further etymology unclear. Since it's often the tên Nôm that bears the original meaning, probably related to etymology 1 (i.e. "villages where [something] grows"), or, again according to folk etymology, from {{m|zh|木}} because the area was once surrounded by woods (i.e. "forest villages"). The earlier {{m|vi|tên chữ}} of the area is Mộc Cự 木巨. I don't really buy into it though since the tên chữ are pretty obviously derivative of the tên Nôm.}}
